    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor typography/Unicode differences (e.g., hyphen vs. true minus, spacing that doesn’t change meaning) could be nitpicks in many tasks, but here the user explicitly required preserving multiplication signs, powers of ten, spaces, superscripts, and inverse-unit exponents exactly as represented, so many “formatting” differences become substantive.\n\nCritical issues:\n1) Table-only constraint violated for names/symbols: The DOM evidence shows the table’s first column contains only symbols (e.g., first row is “Δν”, not “ΔνCs” and no constant name is shown in the table). The agent output adds constant names (e.g., “the caesium hyperfine frequency”) that are not in the table, and alters symbols (ΔνCs vs Δν; NA vs “N A”; Kcd vs “K cd”). Because the task explicitly constrained the agent to use only the table, these additions/alterations are not acceptable.\n2) Exact transcription not met for several value/unit formats per DOM: In DOM-model state 1, multiple rows show values truncated in the captured rendering (e.g., “6.626 070 15 x 10” with no exponent shown; similarly for e, k, N A). The agent output supplies specific exponents (10–34, 10–19, 10–23, and “x 1023”), and adds inverse unit exponents (m s–1, J K–1, mol–1, lm W–1) that are not displayed in the provided table rendering (which shows “m s”, “J K”, “mol”, “lm W”). Given the task’s demand to preserve what is displayed in the table exactly, the agent’s reported table transcriptions do not match the evidence.\n3) One numerical formatting error: For Avogadro, the agent wrote “6.022 140 76 x 1023” (missing the space/superscript formatting implied by scientific notation and inconsistent with the table’s “x 10” style), which is incorrect relative to both the agent’s own claimed formatting goal and the table snippet.\n\nWhat the agent did correctly: It did provide seven items in the correct general conceptual order and it correctly reported the uncertainty statement (“The numerical values of the seven defining constants have no uncertainty.”), which is explicitly supported by DOM-model state 1.\n\nOverall outcome: The primary deliverable was an exact, table-only transcription of the seven constants (symbol/value/unit) as displayed. The agent’s output materially diverges from the displayed table for symbols and for the exact displayed unit/value formatting, and it also includes information (names) not present in the table despite the explicit constraint. Therefore, the task was not successfully completed.",
